1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,433
Last time, this was three balls of rock.

2
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:06,132
Today it's a cave, with a hall somebody built in it,

3
00:00:06,582 --> 00:00:10,004
a haze, a gate, and places with names.

4
00:00:10,904 --> 00:00:12,262
I didn't model any of it.

5
00:00:14,061 --> 00:00:16,452
I added about twenty lines to the same file.

6
00:00:17,652 --> 00:00:21,819
Two of today's fields only show on flat walls,

7
00:00:22,269 --> 00:00:24,438
so the ruin needs one box.

8
00:00:25,338 --> 00:00:28,343
If you did last lecture's exercise, you have it already.

9
00:00:28,793 --> 00:00:30,357
If not, add it now.

10
00:00:31,257 --> 00:00:32,451
It has six numbers:

11
00:00:32,901 --> 00:00:37,673
the middle, then half the width, half the height, half the length.

12
00:00:38,573 --> 00:00:40,526
And it has a passage to the Nave.

13
00:00:41,726 --> 00:00:44,704
This line goes on the ruin, and it names a look.

14
00:00:45,604 --> 00:00:46,758
There are five words.

15
00:00:47,658 --> 00:00:51,179
Rock is asteroids, and it's what you had already.

16
00:00:52,079 --> 00:00:55,038
Plates are flat pieces laid over every wall,

17
00:00:55,488 --> 00:00:57,789
and blocks are the same with thickness.

18
00:00:58,689 --> 00:01:00,890
Ribs are plates with bars across them,

19
00:01:01,340 --> 00:01:02,942
and none is no walls at all.

20
00:01:04,742 --> 00:01:08,166
The game builds a wall from a few hundred small pieces:

21
00:01:08,616 --> 00:01:10,903
about four hundred and fifty rocks for this ruin,

22
00:01:11,353 --> 00:01:13,897
or three hundred and seventy plates.

23
00:01:14,797 --> 00:01:18,329
I'm keeping rock, because this place is a cave.

24
00:01:19,529 --> 00:01:21,905
Now I say only where it changes.

25
00:01:22,805 --> 00:01:25,457
The Gallery was built later, so the Gallery gets blocks.

26
00:01:26,357 --> 00:01:29,223
Every room without a line of its own takes the ruin's,

27
00:01:29,673 --> 00:01:31,998
and so do the tunnels, always.

28
00:01:33,798 --> 00:01:34,815
Now for the Vault.

29
00:01:35,715 --> 00:01:37,402
Art names the piece itself.

30
00:01:37,852 --> 00:01:39,976
The game has six asteroid shapes,

31
00:01:40,426 --> 00:01:42,193
and a rock wall mixes them.

32
00:01:43,093 --> 00:01:45,992
With this line, the Vault is cut from just one.

33
00:01:46,892 --> 00:01:50,073
So Art picks the piece, and Walls picks the look.

34
00:01:51,273 --> 00:01:54,019
Next come three dials, all on the ruin.

35
00:01:54,919 --> 00:01:57,526
Seed decides which rock goes where.

36
00:01:57,976 --> 00:02:01,748
The same number builds the same ruin every time,

37
00:02:02,197 --> 00:02:05,379
so you and your players are looking at the same place.

38
00:02:06,279 --> 00:02:09,898
Debris is the loose rock drifting inside the rooms.

39
00:02:10,348 --> 00:02:13,163
It's sixty if you say nothing, and I want thirty.

40
00:02:14,963 --> 00:02:17,260
Gaps is how much of a built wall is missing.

41
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:21,364
It's a number from zero to one, and not a percentage,

42
00:02:21,814 --> 00:02:24,658
so zero point two is one piece in five.

43
00:02:25,558 --> 00:02:29,069
It only touches flat walls, which here means the Gallery.

44
00:02:30,269 --> 00:02:31,773
One more line on the ruin.

45
00:02:32,673 --> 00:02:35,737
Atmosphere fills the whole place with one cloud,

46
00:02:36,187 --> 00:02:38,431
in one of seven colors.

47
00:02:39,331 --> 00:02:42,524
Leave the line out, or write none, and there's no cloud.

48
00:02:43,724 --> 00:02:45,055
Here's a new kind of record.

49
00:02:45,955 --> 00:02:49,400
It has three hashes and a Relic line, like a room,

50
00:02:49,850 --> 00:02:52,504
but this is a prop, a thing standing in the ruin.

51
00:02:53,404 --> 00:02:55,510
Prop says where it stands,

52
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:59,384
and fourteen hundred along is the middle of the first tunnel.

53
00:03:00,284 --> 00:03:02,112
Dress says what, and how big:

54
00:03:02,562 --> 00:03:04,902
a ring, at four times its size,

55
00:03:05,352 --> 00:03:07,385
which makes it a little wider than the tunnel.

56
00:03:08,285 --> 00:03:11,644
Facing says which way it looks, and that's at the Nave.

57
00:03:13,444 --> 00:03:16,725
A prop takes no space, so you fly straight through it.

58
00:03:17,625 --> 00:03:19,583
These plain shapes come with the game.

59
00:03:20,033 --> 00:03:22,849
Real gates and statues come in an art pack,

60
00:03:23,299 --> 00:03:25,034
and your mission doesn't have one yet.

61
00:03:25,934 --> 00:03:27,395
But you can write a list,

62
00:03:27,845 --> 00:03:30,236
and the game takes the first word it knows.

63
00:03:31,436 --> 00:03:35,217
The last kind of record is a point, which is a named spot.

64
00:03:36,117 --> 00:03:38,556
It has three numbers, inside a room,

65
00:03:39,006 --> 00:03:41,657
and it has roles, which say what it's for.

66
00:03:42,557 --> 00:03:46,038
One role means something to the game, and that's entrance.

67
00:03:46,488 --> 00:03:49,188
The ruin's name on the map moves to this point.

68
00:03:50,988 --> 00:03:53,222
Any other role is a word of my own.

69
00:03:54,122 --> 00:03:56,495
So the Altar goes in the middle of the Vault.

70
00:03:56,945 --> 00:03:59,238
The game stands an invisible marker there,

71
00:03:59,688 --> 00:04:01,264
and when a ship gets close,

72
00:04:01,714 --> 00:04:04,620
it turns into a contact with this name.

73
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:08,218
The Niche is the same, and it's hidden.

74
00:04:09,118 --> 00:04:12,639
Hidden is for a crew in suits, later in this class.

75
00:04:13,089 --> 00:04:15,408
For a ship, it changes nothing.

76
00:04:16,608 --> 00:04:18,617
So I run lint, and it's clean.

77
00:04:19,517 --> 00:04:22,198
Now I misspell a style,

78
00:04:22,648 --> 00:04:25,279
and lint tells me, and asks if I meant blocks.

79
00:04:26,179 --> 00:04:28,044
I take a number out of a point,

80
00:04:28,494 --> 00:04:31,188
and it tells me the place won't be made.

81
00:04:32,988 --> 00:04:37,103
Now I misspell the name of the ring, and lint says clean.

82
00:04:38,003 --> 00:04:40,247
Lint doesn't check that word,

83
00:04:40,697 --> 00:04:43,201
and the game would simply build no ring.

84
00:04:44,101 --> 00:04:47,686
The game does say so, in its log file, after you play.

85
00:04:48,586 --> 00:04:51,875
So read your Dress and Art lines yourself, letter by letter.

86
00:04:53,075 --> 00:04:54,753
The name is at the way in now.

87
00:04:55,653 --> 00:04:57,304
Inside, there's the haze,

88
00:04:57,754 --> 00:05:00,066
and there's the ring, across the tunnel.

89
00:05:00,966 --> 00:05:03,430
Through it we go, and this is the Nave.

90
00:05:05,230 --> 00:05:06,261
Now up to the Vault.

91
00:05:06,711 --> 00:05:09,033
And there's the Altar, on the map,

92
00:05:09,483 --> 00:05:11,116
because I'm close enough.

93
00:05:12,016 --> 00:05:15,770
And this is the Gallery, with built walls, and pieces missing.

94
00:05:16,970 --> 00:05:17,973
Now it's your turn.

95
00:05:18,873 --> 00:05:22,145
Change the Gallery to ribs, and take more of it away.

96
00:05:23,045 --> 00:05:24,205
Put something on the altar,

97
00:05:24,655 --> 00:05:26,525
because a point can be dressed too.

98
00:05:27,425 --> 00:05:28,823
Add a hidden place of your own.

99
00:05:29,723 --> 00:05:32,143
Then break one line where lint can see it,

100
00:05:32,593 --> 00:05:33,968
and one where it can't.

101
00:05:35,768 --> 00:05:38,949
Next time, a place says something when the ship arrives.
